1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,350
This golden coconut is Sri Lanka's very own.

2
00:00:03,390 --> 00:00:05,980
On the island, they call it thambili.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,700
Why does it matter?

4
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:09,500
Traditionally, guests are welcomed

5
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:11,860
with a cool glass of its water.

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,850
And the world wants it too. In 2025,

7
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:19,460
Sri Lanka exported nearly $9 million worth.

8
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,350
About 95% of those exports go to Dubai.

9
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,550
Demand now outpaces supply,

10
00:00:25,590 --> 00:00:28,670
and researchers are working to protect its name.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,940
So what is it?

12
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:33,470
Sri Lanka's coconuts fall into three groups:

13
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:35,550
tall, dwarf, and king.

14
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,400
The king coconut is a semi-tall

15
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,760
palm with bright orange nuts.

16
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,210
Its water is about 95% water,

17
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:47,830
with 5–6 g of natural sugar in every 100 ml.

18
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,700
Potassium is its main mineral:

19
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:52,690
more than half of all the minerals inside.

20
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,330
So how does it reach you?

21
00:00:55,370 --> 00:00:58,160
Nuts are picked 7–8 months after pollination,

22
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,070
when the sugars peak.

23
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:02,260
Count the leaves down from the youngest.

24
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,060
The right bunch hangs at leaf 14.

25
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,980
Within a day and a half, each nut is cleaned,

26
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:10,340
wrapped in film, netted, and packed,

27
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:12,180
6–8 to a box.

28
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,730
Kept at 13–15 °C,

29
00:01:13,770 --> 00:01:17,020
it stays fresh for about 4 weeks.

30
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:20,570
In the tropical heat? Just 4 days.

31
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,570
One orange nut, one island,

32
00:01:23,610 --> 00:01:26,420
and a long, cool journey to your glass.
